# Find in page: Ctrl+F opens the bar, typing counts the matches as you go
# (ASCII case folded), Enter and Shift+Enter walk them and scroll the
# current one into view, editing the query restarts, Escape closes. The
# page is tall enough that the last match sits below the fold.
resize 800 500
open data:text/html,<title>Find</title><style>body{margin:8px;font-family:"Sashfold Mono";font-size:16px;line-height:20px}</style><p>The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.</p><p>x</p><p>x</p><p>x</p><p>x</p><p>x</p><p>x</p><p>x</p><p>x</p><p>x</p><p>x</p><p>x</p><p>x</p><p>x</p><p>x</p><p>Second line: the fox again, and THE end.</p>
assert-title Find
assert-find
key ctrl+f
type the
assert-find 1 of 4
assert-scroll 0
assert-golden goldens/find-first.png
key Enter
assert-find 2 of 4
key Enter
key Enter
assert-find 4 of 4
assert-scrolled
key Enter
assert-find 1 of 4
assert-scroll 0
key shift+Enter
assert-find 4 of 4
type zzz
assert-find No matches
key Backspace
key Backspace
key Backspace
assert-find 1 of 4
key Escape
assert-find
assert-golden goldens/find-closed.png
